 of customers for each type of rice is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}500\\,000 \\\\ 300\\,000 \\\\ 200\\,000\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nDividing the vector above by the total number of customers $(1\\,000\\,000),$ we get the stochastic vector of the initial state:\n\n$$\n{x}_{0}=\\frac{1}{1\\,000\\,000}\\begin{bmatrix}500\\,000 \\\\ 300\\,000 \\\\ 200\\,000\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.5 \\\\ 0.3 \\\\ 0.2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the state vector ${x}_{1}$ after one year, we apply one step of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.7 & 0.3 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.1 & 0.4 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.2 & 0.3 & 0.3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.5 \\\\ 0.3 \\\\ 0.2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.54 \\\\ 0.21 \\\\ 0.25\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after one year, $21\\%$ of customers will buy Type II rice. Computing $21\\%$ of $1\\,000\\,000,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n1\\,000\\,000\\cdot 0.21=210\\,000.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $210\\,000$ customers will buy Type II rice in one year." 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186638235 1074 "The answer choices require interpretation as a percent, and so we use the growth rate formula.\n\nThe given expression is an exponential growth expression of the form $V(t)=a\\cdot (1+r)^{t}$, where:\n\n- $a=1\\,000\\,000$ represents the number of visitors in $2016$\n\n- $1+r=1.5,$ where $r$ is the growth rate\n\n- $t=$ the time since the year $2016$\n\nSolving for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n1+r=1.5\\,⟹\\,r=0.5.\n$$\n\nNow, $0.5$ (expressed as a percent) is equal to $50%.$ Therefore, the number of visitors increased by $50%$ per year." 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186638235 1074 "The answer choices require interpretation as a percent, and so we use the growth rate formula.\n\nThe given expression is an exponential growth expression of the form $V(t)=a\\cdot (1+r)^{t}$, where:\n\n- $a=1\\,000\\,000$ represents the number of visitors in $2016$\n\n- $1+r=1.5,$ where $r$ is the growth rate\n\n- $t=$ the time since the year $2016$\n\nSolving for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n1+r=1.5\\,⟹\\,r=0.5.\n$$\n\nNow, $0.5$ (expressed as a percent) is equal to $50\\%.$ Therefore, the number of visitors increased by $50\\%$ per year." 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186638236 1071 "The migration table below describes the movement of the population between cities, suburbs, and towns every year in a specific state.  \n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\">From:</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Cities</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Suburbs</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Towns</b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"3\">To:</td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Cities</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Suburbs</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"60\"><b>Towns</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.7$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nFor example, $10%$ of those living in towns move to the suburbs each year.\n\nAssuming that the state's population is $10$ million and remains constant, how many people will eventually live in towns if the given probabilities remain constant over many years?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186638236 1071 "The migration table below describes the movement of the population between cities, suburbs, and towns every year in a specific state.  \n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n