\nThe given expression is an exponential growth expression of the form $y(t)=a\\cdot (1+r)^{t}$, where:\n\n- $a=800$ represents the initial population of deer in the wildlife refuge\n\n- $1+r=1.14,$ where $r$ is the growth rate\n\n- $t$ is the number of years since $2000$\n\nSolving for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n1+r=1.14\\,⟹\\,r=0.14.\n$$\n\nNow, $0.14$ (expressed as a percent) is equal to $14\\%.$ Therefore, the deer population grows at a rate of $14\\%$ per year." 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186638255 1071 "The price of a gallon of gasoline is $\\$3.$ Some economists estimate that its price will rise by $1%$ weekly.  Complete the following equation that we should solve to determine how many weeks it will take for the price to increase to $\\$3.5.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\cdot \\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)^{t}=3.5$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186638255 1071 "The price of a gallon of gasoline is $\\$3.$ Some economists estimate that its price will rise by $1\\%$ weekly.  Complete the following equation that we should solve to determine how many weeks it will take for the price to increase to $\\$3.5.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\cdot \\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)^{t}=3.5$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186638255 1074 "The price $y(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $1%.$\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of a growth rate $r$) is\n\n$$\ny=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nFrom the given information, we have the following:\n\n- $a=3$ is the initial price in dollars.\n\n- $r=0.01$ is the growth rate.\n\n- $t$ is the time, in weeks, since the current moment.\n\nSo, the expression for $y(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =3\\cdot (1+0.01)^{t} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (1.01)^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to find the time it takes for the price to increase to $\\$3.5,$ we would need to solve the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =3.5 \\\\ 3\\cdot (1.01)^{t} & =3.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186638255 1074 "The price $y(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $1\\%.$\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of a growth rate $r$) is\n\n$$\ny=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nFrom the given information, we have the following:\n\n- $a=3$ is the initial price in dollars.\n\n- $r=0.01$ is the growth rate.\n\n- $t$ is the time, in weeks, since the current moment.\n\nSo, the expression for $y(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =3\\cdot (1+0.01)^{t} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (1.01)^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to find the time it takes for the price to increase to $\\$3.5,$ we would need to solve the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =3.5 \\\\ 3\\cdot (1.01)^{t} & =3.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186638286 1071 "Andrew deposits $\\$2\\,000$ into a savings account that earns $15%$ interest per year. Complete the following equation that we should solve to determine how many years it will take for the balance in the account to increase to $\\$2\\,400.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\cdot \\,(${{field-2}}$)^{t}=2\\,400$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186638286 1071 "Andrew deposits $\\$2\\,000$ into a savings account that earns $15\\%$ interest per year. Complete the following equation that we should solve to determine how many years it will take for the balance in the account to increase to $\\$2\\,400.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\cdot \\,(${{field-2}}$)^{t}=2\\,400$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186638286 1074 "The investment $y(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $15%.$\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of a growth rate $r$) is\n\n$$\ny=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nFrom the given information, we have the following:\n\n- $a=2\\,000$ is the initial investment, in dollars.\n\n- $r=0.15$ is the growth rate.\n\n- $t$ is the time, in years, since Andrew deposited $\\$2\\,000$ into a savings account.\n\nSo, the expression for $y(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =2\\,000\\cdot (1+0.15)^{t} \\\\  & =2\\,000\\cdot (1.15)^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to find the time it takes for the balance in the account to increase to $\\$2\\,400,$ we would need to solve the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =2\\,400 \\\\ 2\\,000\\cdot (1.15)^{t} & =2\\,400.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186638286 1074 "The investment $y(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $15\\%.$\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of a growth rate $r$) is\n\n$$\ny=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nFrom the given information, we have the following:\n\n- $a=2\\,000$ is the initial investment, in dollars.\n\n- $r=0.15$ is the growth rate.\n\n- $t$ is the time, in years, since Andrew deposited $\\$2\\,000$ into a savings account.\n\nSo, the expression for $y(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =2\\,000\\cdot (1+0.15)^{t} \\\\  & =2\\,000\\cdot (1.15)^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to find the time it takes for the balance in the account to increase to $\\$2\\,400,$ we would need to solve the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =2\\,400 \\\\ 2\\,000\\cdot (1.15)^{t} & =2\\,400.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186638295 1071 "A town with an initial population of $25\\,000$ grows at a rate of $2.5%$ per year. What does the expression  $25\\,000\\cdot (1.025)^{10}$ mean in this context?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186638295 1071 "A town with an initial population of $25\\,000$ grows at a rate of $2.5\\%$ per year. What does the expression  $25\\,000\\cdot (1.025)^{10}$ mean in this context?" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186638299 1074 "The answer choices require interpretation as a percent, and so we use the growth rate formula.\n\nThe given expression is an exponential growth expression of the form $A(t)=a\\cdot (1+r)^{t}$, where:\n\n- $a=5$ represents the initial number of people with allergies\n\n- $1+r=1.25,$ where $r$ is the growth rate\n\n- $t=$ the time since the first cases were reported\n\nSolving for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n