ince the beginning of the observation.\n\nSo, the expression for $y(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =160\\cdot (1+0.17)^{t} \\\\  & =160\\cdot (1.17)^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to find the time it will take for the mouse population to increase to $600,$ we would need to solve the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =600 \\\\ 160\\cdot (1.17)^{t} & =600.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186638309 1074 "The mouse population $y(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $17\\%.$\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of a growth rate $r$) is\n\n$$\ny=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nFrom the given information, we have the following:\n\n- $a=160$ is the initial number of mice.\n\n- $r=0.17$ is the growth rate.\n\n- $t$ is the time, in months, since the beginning of the observation.\n\nSo, the expression for $y(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =160\\cdot (1+0.17)^{t} \\\\  & =160\\cdot (1.17)^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to find the time it will take for the mouse population to increase to $600,$ we would need to solve the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =600 \\\\ 160\\cdot (1.17)^{t} & =600.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186639317 1071 "If\n    $$\n\\displaystyle U=\\begin{bmatrix}-3v & -7 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$\\text{det}(U)=-16$, what is the value of $v?$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186639317 1071 "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle U=\\begin{bmatrix}-3v & -7 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$\\text{det}(U)=-16$, what is the value of $v?$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186639327 1071 "If\n    $$\n\\displaystyle U=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -6 \\\\ -4k & 8k+2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$\\text{det}(U)=-6$, what is the value of $k?$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186639327 1071 "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle U=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -6 \\\\ -4k & 8k+2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$\\text{det}(U)=-6$, what is the value of $k?$" 13194139539448 17592186576